			"notes": "### RyoCraft 1.2\n\n- Kita now appears directly in animated lava pools and lavafalls, while native lava movement and shading remain visible underneath.\n- The bundled Ryo terrain tint now runs through Minecraft's core terrain shaders inside the Ryo Blocks jar.\n- Solid and cutout terrain rendering is now batched more efficiently, with an automatic vanilla fallback whenever a complete compatible batch is unavailable.\n- RyoCraft remains a client-side Fabric mod for Minecraft 1.20.1; vanilla and unmodded servers do not need it installed.\n- Install one file: place `ryo-blocks-1.2.0.jar` in your Fabric 1.20.1 profile's `mods` folder. No separate Fabric API, Iris, Sodium, Indium, OptiFine, or shaderpack is required for normal play."
		},
